{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789384415,"nonce":"rjNeCASuW4Zj940LquKuOkncnnQ=","title":"drop_insert: an allocation a branch decides on is never released","message":"`analyze_site` handed a site whose derived value fed a terminator (a\n`brcond` on `box == null`, the first thing every inlined box reader\ndoes) straight to `MultiBlock` without asking `drop_points` where it\ndies, though the instruction path asks for exactly that shape. So a\nbox read through an inlined `zb_any_as_float` was never freed:\n`bench_any_field.py` allocated a box per iteration and released none,\npeak RSS 96 MB for a million iterations against 50 MB for a program\nthat allocates nothing; the run was 9.5 ms against ZynML's 5.7 for\nthe same kernel.\n\nThe terminator path now goes through `drop_points` under automatic\nrelease like the instruction path; the liveness walk already read\nterminator uses. any_field: 50 MB, 6.3 ms; any_cast the same.\n\n`ZYNTAX_TRACE_DROP=1` now prints each site's outcome and, inside\n`drop_points`, what stopped a release.","files":null}]}